# Why these three lines exist, and what they cost:
# decisions/0139-a-shared-ledger-is-union-merged-and-a-generated-file-is-regenerated.md
#
# Measured on 10 September 2026 with `pnpm queue`, over the thirty open branches:
# 7 of 30 merged into main. With the union line alone, 24. With all three, 28.

# Append-only, and appended to by seven routines that cannot see each other run.
# Both sides are kept; nobody's entry is dropped, and nothing conflicts.
FINDINGS.md merge=union

# Generated. Never resolved by hand — take the tree's copy and regenerate, which
# `pnpm verify` forces by failing on drift. Needs `merge.ours.driver`, which the
# `prepare` script sets on install; without it these conflict as before.
decisions/README.md merge=ours
*.generated.json merge=ours

# Every source file is text, even the one holding a NUL as a key separator.
# `src/data/plan.ts` spent weeks diffing as a pair of byte counts because it
# held the byte literally; the escape fixes that file, and `diff` here fixes the
# class — git calls a file binary when it finds a NUL unless an attribute says
# otherwise.
*.ts text diff
*.tsx text diff
*.md text diff
